  "artifacts": [
    {
      "path": "outputs/rf_model.pkl",
      "type": "Model",
      "description": "Pickled Random Forest regressor trained to predict downstream flow from upstream measurements and their lags."
    },
    {
      "path": "outputs/test_predictions.csv",
      "type": "CSV",
      "description": "CSV file containing actual vs. predicted downstream flow values for the test set, indexed by date."
    }
  ],
  "user_friendly_explanation": "The script loads a prepared time-series dataset of upstream and downstream flow measurements, then splits it chronologically into an 80% training set and a 20% test set. It fits a Random Forest regressor (with 100 trees and a fixed random seed) to predict downstream flow based on the current and three previous upstream flow values. Once training finishes, the model is saved to outputs/rf_model.pkl. The script then runs predictions on the hold-out test period and writes a CSV (outputs/test_predictions.csv) that lists the actual downstream flows alongside the model’s predictions for each test date. You can now use this model file for future forecasts and examine the CSV to compute performance metrics (e.g., RMSE or R²) or visualize prediction accuracy over time."
}

