The successful application of simple lagged‐flow predictors and an ensemble learning algorithm highlights the effectiveness of data‐driven approaches for river discharge forecasting without requiring extensive physical parameterization. By automating data retrieval and feature generation, the workflow is readily adaptable for near‐real‐time operational forecasting in both regulated and unregulated river systems. Future work should explore the integration of meteorological covariates, cross‐basin transferability assessments, and comparisons with alternative machine learning architectures to further enhance forecast skill and robustness.

